Check a Win32 window's pixel format when a session attaches to it with WGL.

Windows lets a window set its pixel format once. Attaching to a window that
already has another one used to return OK and fail later on the session's
thread, while native-abi/render/window_windows expects the attach itself to
fail with MLN_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT, as the C++ library did. The attach
now checks on the caller's thread whenever OpenGL presents to the window.
Upstream: https://github.com/louwers/mln-rs/pull/325, which also carries
0002's fix for WGL custom layers.

